ns.Data.Rotations = {
  assassination = "Icy Veins Assassination (Nov 4, 2026), a priority list: 1) maintain buffs and debuffs: Poisons on both weapons (Instant Poison main hand, Deadly Poison off hand, keep 5 Deadly stacks), Expose Armor if no stronger armor debuff is on the target, Slice and Dice always, Rupture if the target will live through it; 2) open from Stealth with Garrote; 3) Shank on cooldown to keep Venom up (not when Energy is nearly full); 4) Mutilate to build combo points; 5) at 5 combo points Eviscerate if Slice and Dice and Rupture are up and Shank is on cooldown. No AoE. Cooldowns: Cold Blood with a 5-point Eviscerate once threat is established; Vanish for mechanics, threat drop or a Garrote refresh. Leveling (Icy Veins, Nov 18): Instant Poison on both weapons (Crippling Poison for runners), open with Cheap Shot or Garrote, Backstab (Sinister Strike if you can't get behind; Mutilate from 40), Slice and Dice if more targets are coming else Eviscerate at 5 combo points.",
  combat = "Icy Veins Combat (Nov 4, 2026): maintain Poisons (Instant Poison main hand, Deadly Poison off hand), Expose Armor if no stronger armor debuff, Slice and Dice always, Rupture if the target will live; open from Stealth with Garrote; Shank on cooldown if it won't overcap Energy; Sinister Strike to build (Backstab in the dagger variant); at 5 combo points Eviscerate if Slice and Dice and Rupture are up and Shank is on cooldown. Blade Flurry whenever a second target is in range (or on cooldown for its attack speed); Adrenaline Rush after the opening Energy is spent and threat is established; Cold Blood on a 5-point Eviscerate; Vanish for mechanics or a threat drop. Leveling (Icy Veins, Nov 18): Instant Poison on both weapons (Crippling Poison for runners), open with Cheap Shot or Garrote, Riposte whenever it procs, Sinister Strike to build, Slice and Dice if you are confident there will be targets for its duration, else Eviscerate at 5 combo points; Blade Flurry from 30 for two targets.",
  subtlety = "Icy Veins Subtlety (Nov 4, 2026): pool Energy around Death Mark windows. 1) maintain: Instant Poison main hand, Deadly Poison off hand; Rupture (5 combo points), Death Mark (5 combo points), Garrote if the target will live, Slice and Dice (5 combo points); 2) cooldowns: Shank on cooldown at 0-3 combo points (Boot Knife adds 2), Ghostly Strike on cooldown followed by Garrote (Initiative makes it 2 combo points), Premeditation on cooldown; 3) builders: Ambush as the Stealth opener, Hemorrhage as the main builder (30 Energy). Hold Vanish and Preparation for dangerous moments. Don't use multi-point generators at 4 combo points; stand behind the boss. Leveling (Icy Veins, Nov 4): Garrote to open once learned (14), Backstab or Sinister Strike to build until Hemorrhage (30), then Hemorrhage only; Shank and Ghostly Strike on cooldown; Slice and Dice early, Rupture on durable targets from 30, Death Mark as the main finisher from 40 (sample opener: Garrote, Hemorrhage, Shank to 5 combo points, Death Mark, then Hemorrhage and Eviscerate).",
  energy = "Energy regenerates continuously at about 10 per second (Icy Veins; wowfdb: no longer in 2-second ticks); never overcap it. Combo points stay on a target when you switch targets and are lost only when you start building on another enemy or the target dies (Icy Veins, wowfdb). Energy refunds: Shank (+15, +25 at rank 2, Flash of Steel more), Relentless Strikes, Adrenaline Rush; Poised cuts the next ability by 10 Energy when you start a fight at full Energy. Switching specs no longer refills Energy (wowfdb, Oct 16).",
  poisons = "Poisons are learned through the level-20 class quest and are their own skill line; each poison is an item made with that skill and lasts 30 minutes on a weapon. Icy Veins: Instant Poison on the main hand and Deadly Poison on the off hand at endgame; Instant Poison on both weapons while leveling, Crippling Poison for enemies that run. Forever: more charges, poisons can crit (Malice) and use hit (Precision), and Blizzard says a poison can sit on a weapon together with a Sharpening Stone or Weightstone (client data did not show the stacking yet per wowfdb). Venom (via Shank) and Improved Poisons are the Assassination poison talents. Some mobs are immune to poisons (Icy Veins).",
